                                        "entry_id": "dd3f3e18-193a-360f-bfc9-ab0eb004b5c5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In a position of prominence or importance."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9ccf56e5-a2fd-4f66-af72-9162f2201add",
                                                "sense_id": "decd4dcb-b145-307a-a9b7-3459901af94a",
                                                "text": "I'd always considered astrology bullshit, right up there with the legal, real estate and banking businesses in terms of thieving ass-sucking charlatanry, but it's clear I've been doing it a misservice."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e572a93b-75d5-4335-953b-073e76f06396",
                                                "sense_id": "decd4dcb-b145-307a-a9b7-3459901af94a",
                                                "text": "“It is the most reckless challenge on a football pitch I think I’ve ever seen,” said the Palace chairman, Steve Parish, at half-time, going on to talk about the possibility of actually killing a fellow professional.\nIt was certainly up there, with shades of Harald Schumacher at the 1982 World Cup. That was, Schumacher admitted, a deliberate assault designed to stop Patrick Battiston scoring."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b63e65bb-6291-3426-b4ae-413e3687aaac",
                                        "entry_id": "dd3f3e18-193a-360f-bfc9-ab0eb004b5c5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Used other than figuratively or idiomatically: see up, there."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "d6de17e9-a247-4eba-a8ca-55d9b4611ba3",
                        "source_entry_id": "5e2dfc05-1a80-3eb6-8bd1-287441995da5",
                        "source_sense_id": "6c3160d8-7eca-3b03-9822-b27d1a50d15d",
